# CQ 21: Which functional units are composed of others?
#
# Entry 351-56-02 allows a functional unit to consist of further units, and the
# standard uses that in its own definitions: the controller, 351-49-11, is a
# unit consisting of a comparing and a controlling element.
#
# The composition is what lets a model describe the same arrangement at two
# levels. A case may state a controller and stop there, or it may open it up
# and state the two elements inside it, and both are complete descriptions at
# their level.
#
# Reported with the kind of each, since the composition is only readable
# against what the parts are: a controller made of a comparing and a
# controlling element follows the standard, one made of two measuring elements
# does not, and the pattern asserts no such rule.
PREFIX iec60050: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
SELECT ?unit ?unitKind ?partOfIt ?partKind
WHERE {
  ?unit iec60050:consistsOfUnit ?partOfIt .
  ?unit     a ?unitKind . ?unitKind rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:FunctionalUnit .
  ?partOfIt a ?partKind . ?partKind rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:FunctionalUnit .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?unit a ?n1 . ?n1 rdfs:subClassOf+ ?unitKind }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?partOfIt a ?n2 . ?n2 rdfs:subClassOf+ ?partKind }
} ORDER BY ?unit ?partOfIt
